    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45949" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sublĭca</span></b> , ae,
		f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				stake</i> or <i>pile</i> driven into the ground,
				<i>a palisade</i> (cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">palus, sudes, stipes),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. C. 3, 49</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Liv. 23, 37</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vitr. 3,
			3</span></i>.—Esp., of <i>the piles for a
			bridge</i>, 
			<i><span class="en">Caes. B. G.
				4, 17</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7, 35</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 1,
			37</span></i>.—In the form sublices, <i><span class="en">Sall. H. Fragm. 4, 77</span></i>; cf. Gloss.
		Labb.</div>
